      "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #63185\n\n`/v1/responses` returned 400 for `include: [\"web_search_call.results\", \"web_search_call.action.sources\"]`, although the `web_search` tool is accepted. Thanks to the reporter for the clear write-up.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Both values are now accepted. They are ignored, like the other `include` values for built-in tools vLLM does not run.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Before: `ResponsesRequest(input=\"hi\", include=[\"web_search_call.results\", \"web_search_call.action.sources\"])` raised a `literal_error` for `include.0` and `include.1`.\n- New test `test_web_search_include_values_accepted` fails without the fix and passes with it.\n- `tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_protocol.py`, `test_sampling_params.py`, `test_serving_responses.py`, `test_responses_utils.py`: 134 passed, 1 xfailed. `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` clean.\n- Run on an A40 node, but only the pydantic request model was exercised. I did not start a server or run a model, so no end-to-end `curl` check.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: `ResponsesRequest.include` in `vllm/entrypoints/openai/responses/protocol.py` is a closed `Literal` list missing these two values from the OpenAI SDK's `ResponseIncludable`. The fix adds them to the list. I did not switch the field to the SDK type, to keep the diff minimal.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Two literals added to an existing field. No new code paths.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Unit test fails before and passes after. No end-to-end server run.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Matches surrounding code. ruff clean.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Summary, root cause, and evidence included.\n</details>",
